Subject: [PATCH] iommu/qcom: invalidate a newly programmed context

The context bank uses its fixed ASID again after a kexec boot. Programming a
new TTBR does not itself discard cached translations or intermediate table
walks from the previous kernel. Invalidate the context and wait for completion
before publishing the new domain's page-table operations.

On Samsung A5U, successive kexec boots otherwise fault when scanning the third
framebuffer (IOVA 0x732000), despite a valid software page-table walk. Explicit
context invalidation removes these faults and the associated MDP5 underruns.
The existing helper invalidates every context in the domain and synchronizes
completion while the IOMMU clocks are still enabled by attach_dev().

--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -311,6 +311,9 @@
 		ctx->domain = domain;
 	}
 
+	/* Discard cached walks/translations belonging to the previous kernel. */
+	qcom_iommu_tlb_inv_context(qcom_domain);
+
 	mutex_unlock(&qcom_domain->init_mutex);
 
 	/* Publish page table ops for map/unmap */
